# Schwan (M5, D-078): a territorial mute swan (Hoeckerschwan), a beaked diva.
# White w with i shading, k outline, orange bill o with the black knob k and
# black face/eye. Floats: the waterline is sprite row 16 (the body's bottom
# outline); rows 17-23 are the faint underwater body T and paddling feet b.
# idle = calm S-neck, slow head turn (frame 1: shorter bill, head turned).
# telegraph = the hiss: wings arched up over the back like sails (much taller
# than idle), neck drawn back low, bill open (the gap widens in frame 1).
# charge = wings half raised, neck stretched forward low, w bow wave.
# squished = sulking: head tucked under the wing, only a bit of bill shows.
# Faces right, mirror = auto. Hitbox 16x12, bottom centre at the origin.
# Built with a scratch script (shapes + automatic k outline), frozen here.
sprite = schwan
size   = 24x24
origin = 12,20
hitbox = 4,8,16,12
mirror = auto
anim   = idle      frames=2 ticks=30 loop
anim   = telegraph frames=2 ticks=6 loop
anim   = charge    frames=2 ticks=4 loop
anim   = squished  frames=1
